  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 230 AM EDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\n- Northwest flow regime continues with occasional chances for rain\n  with low confidence convection forecast\n\nThe Great Lakes region remains in between an upper high across \nthe western CONUS and longwave troughing across the eastern CONUS \nwith occasional shortwave troughs passing through and bringing \nthe chance for some much-needed rain.\n\nA weakening shortwave trough moves through tonight. Not much \nmoisture available and the best lift is off to the east, so \nlow/slight chance POPs and limited QPF in the current forecast \nlooks good.\n\nThere is inherent low confidence in the details of how things \nplay out Sunday night through Tuesday given the lack of strong\ndynamic lifting mechanism, but instability and shear are \nsufficient for a slow-moving front and weak midlevel vorticity max\nto focus convection across Minnesota/Wisconsin Sunday afternoon \nwhich eventually moves southeast into western Lower Michigan. The \nfailure of the last two similar synoptic scenarios to produce so \nmuch as a lightning strike in our forecast area leads to\nskepticism, but every drought has to end sometime.\n\nThe front moves through Tuesday with fair weather for mid to late\nweek before the longwave upper trough amplifies with a cold \nfront bringing another chance of rain by next weekend.",
